aad7a125d2c"}, "language": "english", "review": "Welcome to Earth Defense Force: a game where you shoot giant bugs, colossal robots, and who knows what else (we’re still not sure) to save the Earth from an “all-out attack” by aliens whose primary goal seems to be making sure your ammo supply runs out. Set in the ultra-plausible near-future-past of 2022, this game promises endless action, intense warfare, and... well, that’s about it.\n\nGameplay is as deep as a kiddie pool. You stand, shoot, and dodge giant space ants that seem far too large to exist in any reality that involves basic biology. The story? Forget about it. It’s just an excuse for more chaos, and the plot’s primary function is to repeatedly shout “STAND AND FIGHT FOR HUMANITY!” in your face like a motivational poster with a machine gun attached.\n\nThe graphics look like they were ripped from a 2007 PowerPoint presentation, and the AI is so predictable that you’ll start to question if the \"enemies\" are actually just cardboard cutouts being moved around by someone off-screen.\n\nIn conclusion, if you're in the mood for a game where the only strategy is shooting until your eyes bleed, The EDF! has you covered. Otherwise, you might want to let Earth fend for itself this time.", "timestamp_created": 1740447723, "timestamp_updated": 1740447723, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.474820166826248169", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1562828575", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 11, "count": 1}]}]}